Track 1: Terminal Loop
- Story & Context: On a freezing November night beneath the Belfast bypass gantry, engineer Kevin Miller watched the central traffic matrix seize control of every red light in the city just as his illegal radio broadcast went live. "We are keeping time with the dying machines," Kevin muttered into the hot microphone while a police cruiser idled blindly below them, unable to move through the gridlocked amber glare. The surprising incident occurred when the hacked signal box began feeding the audio of his bagpipes backward into the city's emergency PA system, turning the highway into a surreal acoustic canyon. This chaotic night of infrastructural rebellion marked the exact birth of the asphalt threnody movement.
